<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Gehrig returns five months after the diagnosis, on the day of his ALS clinic visit. He started his desk role in city public service two weeks ago with the accommodations in place and works four days a week. He sleeps flat, with no breathlessness, morning headaches or daytime sleepiness, but tires after climbing the stairs. His speech slurs more by evening; he coughs once or twice with thin drinks. His weight is down a little further despite extra calories. The power wheelchair has been approved and is due next month. His hepatitis B and C screening tests from the preventive visit were negative, so he is not immune to hepatitis B and continues the vaccine series today. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Work</td><td>Desk role in public service for two weeks; four days a week; accommodations in place</td></tr><tr><td>Breathing</td><td>No orthopnea, morning headaches or daytime sleepiness; tired after stairs</td></tr><tr><td>Speech and swallowing</td><td>More slurring by evening; occasional cough with thin drinks</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>Down a little further</td></tr><tr><td>Results</td><td>Hepatitis B and C screening negative</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

