<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis with progressive limb and bulbar involvement (G12.21)</content>. ALSFRS-R 36. Seated FVC 3.69 L (72%) and supine FVC 63% of predicted, a fall of more than 10% lying down that points to diaphragm weakness; maximal inspiratory pressure -62 cmH2O; no orthopnea. He does not yet meet the criteria for noninvasive ventilation but is close. Weight 86.6 kg, 2.9% below diagnosis. Early swallowing difficulty with thin liquids. ALT 33 U/L. [S]<list><item>Overnight oximetry; noninvasive ventilation fitted as soon as a criterion is met.</item><item>Swallowing study with the speech therapist; chin-tuck and thickened thin liquids as advised.</item><item>Gastrostomy discussed again while FVC is above 50%; he will decide within the next month.</item><item>Continue riluzole; ALT in 3 months.</item><item>Second hepatitis B vaccine dose today.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>ALSFRS-R</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>36 of 48</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Seated forced vital capacity</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>3.69 L, 72% of predicted seated; 63% supine</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Maximal inspiratory pressure; supine capacity and overnight oximetry when values fall or symptoms appear</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Maximal inspiratory pressure -62 cmH2O; supine FVC 63%; overnight oximetry ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Noninvasive ventilation criteria (FVC below 50%, maximal inspiratory pressure weaker than -60 cmH2O, nocturnal desaturation, orthopnea)</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Due</td><td>Not yet met; close on maximal inspiratory pressure; fitting planned as soon as oximetry or tests meet a criterion</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI (gastrostomy discussion if weight falls 5 to 10% or swallowing is unsafe; place while FVC is above 50%)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>86.6 kg, 2.9% below diagnosis; gastrostomy discussed</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Speech and swallowing assessment</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Mild to moderate dysarthria; cough with thin liquids; swallowing study ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive and behavioral screening</td><td>At diagnosis and periodically</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Brief screen repeated in clinic; normal</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression (PHQ-9)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 6</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Symptoms: cramps, spasticity, saliva, emotional lability, pain</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No drooling or emotional lability; cramps controlled</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Mobility, falls, orthoses and equipment</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Orthosis and cane; power wheelchair approved, due next month; no falls</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>ALT on riluzole</td><td>Monthly for 3 months, then every 3 months</td><td>Completed today</td><td>ALT 33 U/L</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Work, disability benefits and social work</td><td>From diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Working four days a week with accommodations</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning</td><td>Early, then at each change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Recorded at the preventive visit; reviewed today with the ventilation and feeding decisions ahead</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Vaccination review</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Influenza and COVID-19 at the preventive visit; second hepatitis B dose today</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>A clear diagnosis, with mimics excluded, within four weeks. Outcome by 1939-05-18: Diagnosis made at two weeks on EMG, MRI and blood tests [S]</item><item>No falls, using an ankle-foot orthosis, a cane, and a safer home. Outcome by 1939-10-19: One fall with an ankle sprain in July, on a day the orthosis was not worn; no falls since it has been worn for all walking outdoors [S]</item><item>Weight held within 5% of the weight at diagnosis. Outcome by 1939-10-19: 89.2 kg at diagnosis and 86.6 kg at five months (2.9% lower) [S]</item><item>Breathing tracked every visit, with noninvasive ventilation started as soon as criteria are met. Outcome by 1939-10-19: FVC 72% and no symptoms at five months; overnight oximetry ordered [S]</item><item>Goals of care, a health care agent, and his wishes about ventilation and feeding recorded early and revisited. Outcome by 1939-09-21: Agent named and wishes recorded at the preventive visit [S]</item><item>Working in a role that suits him, with accommodations. Outcome by 1939-10-19: Started a desk role in public service with accommodations [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), second of two doses [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: drug, nutritional, and respiratory therapies (an evidence-based review) (2009); Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: multidisciplinary care, symptom management, and cognitive/behavioral impairment (an evidence-based review) (2009); The ALSFRS-R: a revised ALS functional rating scale that incorporates assessments of respiratory function (1999); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Overnight oximetry and swallowing study within two weeks; respiratory therapist to fit noninvasive ventilation when a criterion is met. Decision on gastrostomy within a month. ALS clinic in about two months. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
